{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py::test_code_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union`\nfailed CI on the checked `git push origin HEAD:tickets` in `_assert_emit_is_append_only`\n(currently line 1738), costing Gerrit change 1655 a spurious `Verified -1`.\n\n## The filed premise is FALSIFIED (evidence in comments)\n\nFiled hypothesis: a lost CAS / non-fast-forward between two clones racing the push leg. The\njob's captured log disproves it. The push was rejected by the RECEIVING repository with\n`unresolved deltas left after unpacking`, `remote unpack failed: unpack-objects abnormal\nexit`, and `refs/heads/tickets does not point to a valid object!` — the remote rejected the\npack as an unpacker error. There is no `non-fast-forward`, no `cannot lock ref`, and no\nOOM/signal anywhere in the job. The same warning repeats 18 times with a monotonically\nclimbing unpushed-commit counter, so the fixture's bare `remote.git` was already missing\nobjects from the FIRST emit push onward: the remote was corrupt before any assertion ran.\n\nThis is object loss inside the fixture's own remote, not a ref race between the two clones.\nThe earlier sibling occurrence failed differently (an empty clone-B event set, root-caused\nand fixed by willing-cellular-carp), so the two are distinct mechanisms.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThree facts compose:\n\n1. `two_clones` creates the bare remote with a plain `git init --bare` (line 216) and never\n   configures it.\n2. `_make_repo` clones that local path with no `--no-hardlinks` (line 66), so repo A/B\n   `.git/objects` are HARDLINKED to `remote.git/objects`, and `.tickets-tracker` is a linked\n   worktree sharing repo A's object database (`_commands/init.py:381`).\n3. rebar's gc-config ensure unit (`_commands/init.py:112-155`) deliberately re-enables\n   auto-gc but forces it FOREGROUND (`gc.autoDetach=false`, `maintenance.autoDetach=false`),\n   precisely because a DETACHED background gc/maintenance repacking an object database\n   outside the write lock corrupts the store (bug 88eb, ADR 0051; `_store/sync.py:17-26`).\n\nThat pinning reaches the tracker and its enclosing clone. It does NOT reach the bare remote.\n`remote.git` is therefore the one repository in the fixture whose `receive-pack` runs\n`git gc --auto` at git's defaults — DETACHED — after each of the ~50 emit pushes, repacking\nand pruning its object store concurrently with the next incoming push. git-clone(1) also\nwarns that local hardlink clones can race with concurrent modification of the source\nrepository, which is exactly the shape here.\n\n## Scope\n\nFixture/test-only; no `src/rebar` behaviour change. Fixing it at the remote-creation and\nclone sites covers all 16 `push … HEAD:tickets` sites in this file at once.\n\nReconciled with depraved-frowzy-trout: that audit classified read-sync preconditions\n(`_expire_sync_marker` to `_sync_from_origin`). It did not classify push sites, so there is\nno kept-as-fail-fast decision being overturned here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 — The fixture's bare remote is pinned to the same no-detached-upkeep posture rebar\n      pins on trackers, and the clones no longer hardlink its object store. The reason is\n      recorded at the fixture with the bug 88eb / ADR 0051 reference.\n- [x] AC2 — A regression test asserts that posture on the fixture's remote, so a future\n      fixture that drops the pin fails deterministically here rather than rarely in CI.\n- [x] AC3 — Fail-fast preserved: a genuinely failing push still fails. Proven by a test that\n      makes the remote reject a push and asserts the fixture's push path still raises. No\n      retry, no swallowed error, and no wall-clock bound is introduced.\n- [x] AC4 [operator-attested] — The affected file passes at least 20 consecutive runs under CI's settings\n      (`-n 4 --dist loadgroup`), with the evidence recorded in a comment.\n- [x] AC5 [operator-attested] — `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786570576081861001,"uuid":"442d98bb-8ff4-4c8a-9709-6faba4da0381"}